I don't know, I think I might actually agree with dogscoff here. The
serial demigods definitely make _fewer_ mistakes, but I am certain there
are a number of mistakes per game; one of the marks of a serial ascender
in my mind is the ability to think hard and make the optimal moves when
it really counts, and _recover from mistakes._ This is why you rarely or
never see serial ascenders have mid- or late-game deaths; by then, they
have the resources to recover from their mistakes where a lesser player
would not know how to use them and a lazier player would not bother.

>> The game designer can use that: Encourage the player to make mistakes. 
